Spec: Todo Item Component

Purpose:
  Render a single todo with toggle and remove controls.

Owns:
  todo-item.js

Must:
  Display the todo title.
  Reflect completed state visually (e.g. strikethrough or checked checkbox).
  Invoke onToggle with the todo id when the toggle control is activated.
  Invoke onRemove with the todo id when the remove control is activated.

Must not:
  Call TodoService directly.
  Modify the todo object.
  Access localStorage.

Accepts:
  todo: Todo
  onToggle(id) callback
  onRemove(id) callback

Scenario: toggle interaction
  Given a rendered todo item
  When the user activates the toggle control
  Then onToggle is called with the todo's id

Scenario: remove interaction
  Given a rendered todo item
  When the user activates the remove control
  Then onRemove is called with the todo's id

Scenario: completed visual state
  Given a todo with completed = true
  When the item renders
  Then the completed style is applied to the title

Done when:
  onToggle and onRemove fire with the correct id.
  Completed state is reflected in the rendered output.
  No service or storage imports exist.
